If you are setting std.lv <http://std.lv> = FALSE, then fixing the first loadings to 1 in the syntax is redundant (read the ?lavaan help page and the tutorial pages: http://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/cfa.html).  Not knowing anything about the model fit in Amos, I can't say why your df differ, but your model is identified.  And the model runs without error -- just a warning about a Heywood case.  You can search for information about that on Google or an introductory text on SEM / CFA.

Terry

